1. Create .h files for all the tasks (i.e., clock_task, tty_task, etc.) for defines, includes, and function prototypes.
2. Include the .h files for the tasks in relevant source files.
3. Fill in the executable code for all the tasks.
4. Fill in the executable code for the ready() function in proc.c, which needs lock().
5. Build a cross compiler for i386 target and start cross compiling MyNIX.
6. Get MyNIX working in QEMU as quickly as possible for testing.
